  "query_preview": ".. (Sunday Night through Friday)\n\nUpper-level height rises and an amplifying western ridge will\nbuild into the Great Lakes region early next week, marking a \nswift transition back to seasonably warm, dry, and pleasant \nsummer weather for Monday and Tuesday. High temperatures will \ncomfortably rebound into the mid-80s beneath mostly sunny skies.\n\nThe next opportunity for organized precipitation arrives mid-\nweek as a robust northern-stream shortwave drives a cold front\ntoward the Upper Midwest. Guidance exhibits considerable spread\nregarding how far south this boundary can penetrate into \ncentral Illinois as its parent upper-level dynamics rapidly \ndisplace eastward into Canada. Will maintain conservative 20-30%\nPoPs for Wednesday through Thursday to account for these timing\nand boundary-position uncertainties. \n\nHowever, recent deterministic and ensemble guidance hints at a\nsecondary reinforcing shortwave digging across the Plains and \nriding along the quasistationary surface boundary Thursday. This\nwould increase local baroclinicity and reinvigorate the cold \nfront, driving it southward across the local forecast area. This\nlatter scenario would favor higher probabilities for showers \nand thunderstorms during the Thursday into Friday timeframe and \nwill bear watching in future guidance updates.",
